# DEEPTECH-PARALLEL-013 §10 — local, scoped negation. Nothing here changes global behaviour:
# a .gitignore is consulted only for paths at or below its own directory, so every pattern
# below is inert outside research/deeptech-operations/.
#
# WHY. The repository root .gitignore carries 51 `*.md` patterns aimed at generated
# operational prose. Five of them match names this research programme uses as SOURCE:
#
#   .gitignore:50  *_CHECKLIST.md     (OPERATOR_CHECKLIST.md)
#   .gitignore:51  *_READINESS*.md    (REGISTRATION_READINESS_PACKAGE.md, REGISTRATION_READINESS_TABLE.md)
#   .gitignore:55  *_REPORT.md        (the DEEPTECH_PARALLEL_0NN_REPORT.md series)
#   .gitignore:58  *_RUNBOOK*.md
#   .gitignore:77  ROLE_*.md          (ROLE_DESCRIPTIONS.md)
#
# A bulk `git add research/deeptech-operations` drops every match SILENTLY and exits 0.
# That is how a wave's output gets committed, so the loss is the default outcome.
#
# One line fixes the whole class. An enumerated five-pattern negation was rejected: it
# leaves the other ~46 `.md` patterns armed for the next wave, and fails the same silent
# way. Markdown under this directory is source by construction; nothing generated lives here.
!*.md

# NOT NEGATED — DELIBERATE. `.gitignore:12 *.log` still hides MUTATION_RUN.log and every
# other certification log under this tree. Whether mutation-run logs belong in git is a
# separate and narrower question (size, churn, whether a log is evidence or a by-product)
# and is recorded as OWNER DECISION REQUIRED, not decided here. Until it is decided, name
# such a file explicitly on the command line (`git add -f <path>`), which fails loudly
# rather than silently, or keep it out of git.
